  "result": "I added `clamp(cents: int, low: int, high: int) -> int` to `shop/money.py`. It returns `cents` held within `low..high`, bounds included, and raises `ValueError` when `low > high`. When `low == high` it just returns that value.\n\nThere was no test file for `money.py`, so I created `tests/test_money.py` in the same `unittest` style as `tests/test_pricing.py`. The tests check:\n- a value inside the range\n- values below and above it\n- values exactly on each bound\n- `low == high`\n- `low > high` raising the error\n\nThe full suite passes: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` ran 12 tests, all OK. Nothing is committed.",
